+# Response-aware legal code learning for the selected dialogue child
+
+The selected FullPrefix child now has an offline alpha-learning path over its
+existing integer grids, a separate learned-code artifact schema, and explicit
+development and native-output observers. Seventeen focused engineering checks
+pass. Eight actual training normalization presentations completed with zero
+optimizer updates. The selected 512-update fit subsequently stopped at190 updates
+when its frozen shared-storage guard fired, before any alpha checkpoint. Its
+language outcome is unavailable. The [interruption record](../evidence/dialogue-code-choice-interruption-2026-09-27.json)
+preserves all failed cost and the next operational correction. The preparation
+and prospective selection below remain their dated evidence, not model promotion.
+
+The [evidence packet](../evidence/dialogue-code-choice-preparation-2026-09-27.json)
+includes the executed checks and their failed fixture, normalization results,
+source and executable bindings, independent objective/recipe reviews, complete
+resource cursor, and the prospectively selected fit contract. The causal basis
+is the [same-child native observation](dialogue-child-native-observation-2026-09-27.md):
+nearest conversion lost Momo and green, plus partial teacher/July/piano answers,
+while most additional interface/integer numerical changes were small.
+
+## Implemented path and fixed conditions
+
+Source `34964512fd092a639000f8c4061bc0b8f41b862a` keeps the original continuous
+child and sealed nearest conversion intact. It imports those exact exported
+grids without recalibration, independently loads the child, and projects only
+out-of-range working shadows. Original fractional positions remain available
+to the existing neighboring-code relaxation. Both the parameter quantizer and
+the alpha operator's initial hard arrays must equal the nearest control.
+
+Only alpha variables learn. Complete-prefix response/EOS gradients are combined
+by supervised-token mass across two shards before adding one global rounding
+penalty and making one clipped Adam update. Earlier context remains in the
+gradient graph. Checkpoints save alpha, Adam, exact data schedule and recipe.
+Export reopens the sealed checkpoint and reconstructs its actual saved choices;
+it cannot relabel a learned artifact as a zero-update conversion. Portable
+bundle validation does not open historical training or optimizer paths.
+
+The continuous child's model clock remains 1,024; alpha has its own clock.
+Model width is 576, read-vector width 64, training/evaluation context 256,
+with full causal access, Quaternion transport, Dot reading and vocabulary 4,096.
+Read-vector width does not limit accessible history. Existing dense parameter
+access remains; this is no D5 selected-access result or change of serving
+arithmetic. The native, multiplier-free serving target remains authoritative.
+
+```text
+dialogue-child-rounding --normalize CAMPAIGN NEW_REPORT_ROOT
+dialogue-child-rounding CAMPAIGN NEW_REPORT_ROOT
+dialogue-child-rounding --evaluate CAMPAIGN PACKED_ROOT NEW_REPORT_ROOT
+dialogue-integer-observe --child-rounded CHILD_REPORT_ROOT CORPUS_MANIFEST TOKENIZER PACKED_ROOT BUNDLE_ROOT REQUESTS CHILD_RESPONSES NEW_REPORT_ROOT
+```
+
+The endpoint scorer admits the exact nearest or learned artifact and reuses the
+child's original 161-response development panel, batch four, without reselection.
+It reports QQ F32 emulation. The native observer separately retains the original
+continuous FF reference and observes learned QF/QQ/integer values and all 58
+dialogue turns. The fixed controller, request IDs, tokenizer and protocol remain
+unchanged. This previously exposed development population is not a fresh final
+holdout, and its completions are not added to training labels.
+
+## Executed validation and normalization
+
+Five learning/artifact checks pass, covering response-weighted full-prefix
+gradients, a single global penalty, immutable parent, resumable alpha/Adam,
+pooled normalization, actual saved-code export and strict lineage. Eight integer
+checks and four observer checks pass, and both training examples plus the integer
+binary compile offline in release mode. These checks establish their engineering
+contracts, not language. The first integer run's new negative test changed the
+first parameter's valid shape `[1]` to `[1]`; that no-op fixture was corrected
+to `[999]`. Production validation was already correct. The original failure is
+preserved. Both build/check attempts total 652.200 seconds; the successful second
+attempt takes 332.165 seconds. No blanket suite was added.
+
+The normalization uses eight B16×T256 initial-soft training presentations from
+counter 1,024 with inherited seed 20260929. It processes 128 response/EOS visits,
+9,179 supervised targets and 32,768 padded positions. It performs zero optimizer
+updates and uses no evaluation data. Pooled task-gradient L2 is 0.005416987245;
+unit beta-two penalty-gradient L2 is 0.000183211734. Their ratio selects
+`29.56681391929494`. This initialization heuristic neither establishes an optimal
+coefficient nor balances gradients throughout the changing beta schedule.
+
+Normalization takes 60.256 seconds inside Rust and 61.107 seconds for the entire
+supervised process, with peak child RSS 6,919,520,256 bytes. Batch times average
+6.935 seconds and peak at 7.879 seconds. These observations exclude Adam and
+the later annealed penalty; multiplying them by a dose is a planning reference,
+not a runtime bound. The original grids, model and nearest artifact remain
+unchanged. No automatically executable fit recipe is emitted by normalization.
+
+## Selected experiment and outcome decisions
+
+The principal selects one 512-update recipe: Adam learning rate 0.01, zero
+weight decay, global clip one, 102 penalty-free warmup updates, then the existing
+cosine beta schedule from 20 toward two with the measured coefficient. This
+reuses an exercised optimizer/schedule without inheriting the old width-256
+coefficient or claiming its NLL improvement preserved complete replies.
+The stream continues at counters 1,024–1,535. Its 8,192 response visits and
+2,097,152 padded positions are additional adaptation; actual supervised targets
+must be measured. The normalization's 9,179 targets are additional backward
+presentations, separate from these optimizer exposures.
+
+A checkpoint at update 256 and a final checkpoint preserve the run. The fit's
+soft wall is 5,400 seconds, hard wall 5,520, and complete phase 5,760 including
+preflight and closeout. RSS stays within 8 GiB and new fit material within
+512 MiB. The prospective complete plan also reserves 600 seconds for both
+fixed-panel endpoints, packaging and native observation, and 1,800 seconds for
+review/delivery. It fits the existing cumulative allowance; no global limit,
+paid compute or destructive cleanup is introduced.
+
+The fixed endpoints will compare nearest and learned QQ on the original 161
+responses, then inspect every actual native reply against both nearest and
+continuous output. Useful complete relations and all-output tradeoffs determine
+retention. Lower NLL, isolated keywords or changed stopping counts alone do not
+qualify a repair. A mixed/negative result is preserved and changes the next
+implementation; it does not trigger an automatic dose, seed, scale or decoder
+sweep. A resource stop preserves a checkpoint and is not model-quality evidence.
+
